    "forensics": "The losing cluster splits into two distinct failure modes: morning liquidity sweeps getting whipsawed out at exactly the 0.68% stop-loss floor (INFY, ITC, TATASTEEL), and late-afternoon entries (13:45-14:10) lacking the momentum to reach an overly ambitious 1.65% target before the EOD square-off. Notably, the strategy generated a positive gross P&L (+\u20b918.32), meaning the -\u20b916.56 net loss is entirely driven by transaction fee drag (\u20b934.88) on stalled afternoon trades and premature stop-outs.",
    "learning": "In NSE large-cap cash equities, intraday alpha decays rapidly after 13:30 IST due to tapering institutional participation and rising regulatory fee drag on stagnant positions; surviving morning volatility requires a wider structural stop-loss buffer (0.74%) paired with stricter volume confirmation (2.85x), while targets must be calibrated to achievable intraday ADR (1.35%) with an earlier breakeven lock (0.85R) to protect gross gains from EOD decay.",
